<title>UK: E&amp;G reshuffles UK estate with Canada Life.</title>
<headline>E&amp;G reshuffles UK estate with Canada Life.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>British property company Estates &amp; General Plc said on Thursday it had agreed to buy a portfolio of UK office and industrial properties from Canada Life Assurance Company for a total price of 13.23 million stg.</p>
<p>It is also selling to Canada Life a British development site for 1.0 million.</p>
<p>&quot;On a proforma annualised basis, the acquisition and the disposal are, when taken together, expected to benefit operating income by an amount in excess of 500,000 stg,&quot; E &amp; G said.</p>
</text>
